# Line endings are LF, in the index and in every working tree (wolf-std#15).
# This repository was the only one in the org without the line, and it is
# the one whose gauntlet compares generated `.lu` bytes: `gen-vectors
# --check` canonicalizes the emitter's output through `wolf fmt` (D34) and
# then compares it against the committed file, so a windows checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` would hand CRLF files to an LF comparison.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ...except the vendored vector corpora, which are byte-verbatim (hashes
# in vendor/vectors/README.md); git must never normalize their line
# endings, and the CAVP `.rsp` files really are CRLF upstream. Last
# matching line wins, so this must stay BELOW the rule above.
vendor/vectors/** -text
